#: ../../source/iconv-lite_README.md:94
msgid "Supported encodings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iconv-lite_README.md:96
msgid ""
"All node.js native encodings: utf8, ucs2 / utf16-le, ascii, binary, "
"base64, hex."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iconv-lite_README.md:97
msgid "Additional unicode encodings: utf16, utf16-be, utf-7, utf-7-imap."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iconv-lite_README.md:98
msgid ""
"All widespread singlebyte encodings: Windows 125x family, ISO-8859 "
"family,  IBM/DOS codepages, Macintosh family, KOI8 family, all others "
"supported by iconv library.  Aliases like 'latin1', 'us-ascii' also "
"supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iconv-lite_README.md:101
msgid ""
"All widespread multibyte encodings: CP932, CP936, CP949, CP950, GB2312, "
"GBK, GB18030, Big5, Shift_JIS, EUC-JP."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iconv-lite_README.md:103
msgid ""
"See [all supported encodings on wiki](https://github.com/ashtuchkin"
"/iconv-lite/wiki/Supported-Encodings)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iconv-lite_README.md:105
msgid ""
"Most singlebyte encodings are generated automatically from [node-"
"iconv](https://github.com/bnoordhuis/node-iconv). Thank you Ben Noordhuis"
" and libiconv authors!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iconv-lite_README.md:107
msgid ""
"Multibyte encodings are generated from [Unicode.org "
"mappings](http://www.unicode.org/Public/MAPPINGS/) and [WHATWG Encoding "
"Standard mappings](http://encoding.spec.whatwg.org/). Thank you, "
"respective authors!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iconv-lite_README.md:110
msgid "Encoding/decoding speed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iconv-lite_README.md:112
msgid ""
"Comparison with node-iconv module (1000x256kb, on MacBook Pro, Core "
"i5/2.6 GHz, Node v0.12.0).  Note: your results may vary, so please always"
" check on your hardware."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iconv-lite_README.md:120
msgid "BOM handling"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iconv-lite_README.md:122
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Decoding: BOM is stripped by default, unless overridden by passing "
"`stripBOM: false` in options (f.ex. `iconv.decode(buf, enc, {stripBOM: "
"false})`). A callback might also be given as a `stripBOM` parameter - "
"it'll be called if BOM character was actually found."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iconv-lite_README.md:125
msgid ""
"If you want to detect UTF-8 BOM when decoding other encodings, use [node-"
"autodetect-decoder-stream](https://github.com/danielgindi/node-"
"autodetect-decoder-stream) module."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iconv-lite_README.md:126
msgid "Encoding: No BOM added, unless overridden by `addBOM: true` option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iconv-lite_README.md:128
msgid "UTF-16 Encodings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iconv-lite_README.md:130
msgid ""
"This library supports UTF-16LE, UTF-16BE and UTF-16 encodings. First two "
"are straightforward, but UTF-16 is trying to be smart about endianness in"
" the following ways:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iconv-lite_README.md:132
msgid ""
"Decoding: uses BOM and 'spaces heuristic' to determine input endianness. "
"Default is UTF-16LE, but can be  overridden with `defaultEncoding: 'utf-"
"16be'` option. Strips BOM unless `stripBOM: false`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iconv-lite_README.md:134
msgid ""
"Encoding: uses UTF-16LE and writes BOM by default. Use `addBOM: false` to"
" override."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iconv-lite_README.md:136
msgid "Other notes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iconv-lite_README.md:138
msgid ""
"When decoding, be sure to supply a Buffer to decode() method, otherwise "
"[bad things usually happen](https://github.com/ashtuchkin/iconv-lite/wiki"
"/Use-Buffers-when-decoding).   Untranslatable characters are set to � or "
"?. No transliteration is currently supported.   Node versions 0.10.31 and"
" 0.11.13 are buggy, don't use them (see #65, #77)."
msgstr ""

